The bug is in `withClient` (db.js:11-16):

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  const result = await fn(client);
  client.release();
  return result;
}
```

If `fn(client)` throws, `client.release()` is skipped and that connection is held forever. Each failed query permanently shrinks the effective pool until it's exhausted — which lines up with the `error: timeout exceeded when trying to connect` at 14:04:11.

Fix by releasing in a `finally`:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

